      "problem": "If $y(t)=A\\cdot {5}^{t}$ and $y(2)=175,$ then $A=$",
      "worked_solution": "We substitute $t=2$ and $y(t)=175$ into the expression for $y(t)$ and then solve for $A,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}175 & =A\\cdot {5}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{175}{{5}^{2}} & =A \\\\ \\frac{175}{25} & =A \\\\ 7 & =A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=7.$",
